---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="ArkheionX — Review maps for smart contract security"
  description="ArkheionX turns Solidity and Foundry repositories into deterministic review maps for human security researchers."
>
  <main class="vc-home">
    <section class="vc-hero">
      <div class="vc-hero__inner">
        <div class="vc-hero__copy">
          <p class="vc-kicker">FOR SECURITY TEAMS REVIEWING DEFI CODE</p>

          <h1>A review map for smart contracts.</h1>

          <p class="vc-lede">
            <strong>Foundry tells you whether the tests you wrote pass. ArkheionX helps show the
            value paths you may have forgotten to test.</strong>
          </p>

          <p class="vc-lede">
            ArkheionX turns a local Solidity or Foundry repository into a structured review map:
            who can move value, where trust assumptions live, which tests are missing, and what
            changed between review runs.
          </p>

          <div class="vc-one-line">
            <span>Input</span>
            <strong>Smart contract repo</strong>
            <span>Output</span>
            <strong>Deterministic review context</strong>
            <span>Decision</span>
            <strong>Human reviewer</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="vc-install-card">
            <div class="vc-install-card__top">
              <span>Install from source</span>
              <span>public main</span>
            </div>
            <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://arkheionx.dev/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="vc-note">
            Source install is available. Binary releases are not published yet.
            Inspect-first and manual install paths are documented on the Install page.
          </p>

          <div class="vc-actions">
            <a class="vc-button vc-button--primary" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
            <a class="vc-button" href="/install">Install guide</a>
            <a class="vc-button" href="https://github.com/Yudis-bit/DeFi-Exploit-PoCs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="vc-artifact" aria-label="Review map artifact preview">
          <div class="vc-artifact__top">
            <span>Review map</span>
            <span>local / deterministic</span>
          </div>

          <div class="vc-artifact__body">
            <div class="vc-artifact__row">
              <span class="vc-artifact__label">Contracts</span>
              <strong>Vault · Strategy · Oracle · Token</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="vc-artifact__row">
              <span class="vc-artifact__label">Roles</span>
              <strong>Owner · Keeper · User · Emergency admin</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="vc-artifact__row">
              <span class="vc-artifact__label">Value paths</span>
              <strong>deposit → invest → divest → withdraw</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="vc-artifact__row">
              <span class="vc-artifact__label">Assumptions</span>
              <strong>Oracle freshness · Access control · Accounting invariant</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="vc-artifact__row">
              <span class="vc-artifact__label">Test gaps</span>
              <strong>withdraw · emergencyWithdraw · setOracle</strong>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="vc-artifact__mini">
            <div>
              <span>Source fingerprints</span>
              <strong>tracked</strong>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span>Snapshot drift</span>
              <strong>checked</strong>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span>RPC</span>
              <strong>off by default</strong>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span>Review result</span>
              <strong>human required</strong>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-proof">
      <span>Public-safe source</span>
      <span>Local-first</span>
      <span>No RPC by default</span>
      <span>No private keys</span>
      <span>Snapshot drift checks</span>
      <span>Human review required</span>
    </section>


    <section class="vc-artifact-map">
      <div class="vc-artifact-map__copy">
        <p class="vc-kicker">What the review map captures</p>
        <h2>One repository becomes a structured security review surface.</h2>
        <p>
          ArkheionX does not try to replace the reviewer. It organizes the context a reviewer
          needs before making a judgment: permissions, value movement, assumptions, test gaps,
          evidence, and drift between runs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="artifact-map-visual" aria-label="ArkheionX review artifact map">
        <div class="artifact-map-visual__input">
          <span>Input</span>
          <strong>Solidity / Foundry repository</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="artifact-map-visual__engine">
          <span>ArkheionX</span>
          <strong>Local deterministic mapping</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="artifact-map-visual__outputs">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <strong>Roles</strong>
            <p>Who can act?</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <strong>Value paths</strong>
            <p>Where can funds move?</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <strong>Assumptions</strong>
            <p>What must stay true?</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>04</span>
            <strong>Test gaps</strong>
            <p>What is not covered?</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>05</span>
            <strong>Evidence</strong>
            <p>What supports review?</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>06</span>
            <strong>Drift</strong>
            <p>What changed?</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-section vc-section--intro">
      <div>
        <p class="vc-kicker">What problem does this solve?</p>
        <h2>Security review loses context.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="vc-copy">
        <p>
          A smart contract reviewer needs to understand permissions, value movement, dependencies,
          assumptions, test coverage, and evidence before making a judgment. That context is often
          rebuilt manually and inconsistently.
        </p>
        <p>
          ArkheionX makes the review surface explicit and repeatable, so teams can compare what
          changed instead of rebuilding the same mental model from scratch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-section">
      <div class="vc-heading">
        <p class="vc-kicker">How it works</p>
        <h2>From codebase to review context.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="vc-flow">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Read the local repo</h3>
          <p>Start from Solidity and Foundry source files on your machine.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Build a protocol map</h3>
          <p>Organize contracts, roles, value paths, assumptions, and test gaps.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Record artifacts</h3>
          <p>Produce deterministic, JSON-safe review context that can be inspected.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Compare drift</h3>
          <p>Use fixture benchmarks, fingerprints, and snapshots to detect changes.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>Review manually</h3>
          <p>Use the output as evidence context. A human still makes the security call.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-section">
      <div class="vc-heading">
        <p class="vc-kicker">Why it matters</p>
        <h2>Less noise. More review structure.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="vc-cards">
        <article>
          <h3>For security researchers</h3>
          <p>Keep a repeatable map of what matters before writing findings or reports.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>For audit teams</h3>
          <p>Standardize review context across reviewers, revisions, and protocol versions.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>For protocol engineers</h3>
          <p>Pre-review assumptions, test gaps, and value paths before external review.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>For future automation</h3>
          <p>Build reliable review infrastructure before trusting automated conclusions.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-section vc-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="vc-kicker">Try it locally</p>
        <h2>Start with the review map.</h2>
        <p>
          Real output from the bundled demo — not hardcoded, and locked by tests. Each test gap
          carries a <code>Source: &lt;file&gt;:&lt;line&gt;</code> so you can open the exact function.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="vc-command-list">
        <pre><code>arkheionx version</code></pre>
        <pre><code>arkheionx doctor</code></pre>
        <pre><code>arkheionx review-map .</code></pre>
        <pre><code>arkheionx review-map examples/vault-strategy-oracle-fixture</code></pre>
        <pre><code>OK    Map review surface  3 contracts, 14 functions, 3 value paths, 5 test gaps

Inspect first
1  HIGH   Strategy.divest            Signals  external-call, value-out
2  HIGH   Vault.emergencyWithdraw    Signals  external-call, privileged, value-out
3  HIGH   Vault.withdraw             Signals  external-call, value-out

Test gap   Vault.withdraw   Source  src/Vault.sol:63   Proof  proof-vault-withdraw</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-section vc-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="vc-kicker">Current status</p>
        <h2>Public source is available. Distribution is still being hardened.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="vc-status-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Available now</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Public-safe source branch</li>
            <li>Local source install path</li>
            <li>Fixture benchmark harness</li>
            <li>Source fingerprints</li>
            <li>Snapshot drift checks</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Not yet available</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Prebuilt binary releases</li>
            <li>Hosted dashboard</li>
            <li>Automatic vulnerability confirmation</li>
            <li>Audit certification</li>
            <li>Public bounty submission workflow</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vc-boundary">
      <p class="vc-kicker">Safety boundary</p>
      <h2>ArkheionX is not an auditor.</h2>
      <p>
        ArkheionX creates review context. It does not confirm vulnerabilities, assign final
        severity, prove protocol safety, submit reports, or stand in for human security review.
      </p>
      <a class="vc-button" href="/docs/safety-model">Read the safety model</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
